<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">How often should conveyor PM be performed?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Daily: visual inspection, tracking check, debris removal. Weekly: tension check, roller spin test, sensor test. Monthly: bearing lubrication, motor temperature. Quarterly: drive inspection, electrical connections. Annually: full inspection, motor insulation test, controls backup. Food-grade and high-speed lines need more frequent PM.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">How do I track a conveyor belt?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Run the belt empty. If it drifts right, tighten the right-side tail pulley bolt by 1/4 turn. Wait 3-5 revolutions. Repeat with small adjustments until centered. Then load product and verify. If tracking does not respond, check for material buildup on pulleys, belt damage, splice failure, or frame misalignment.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What causes a conveyor belt to slip?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Five causes: insufficient belt tension (increase tension), wet or contaminated drive pulley (clean it), worn pulley lagging (replace it), overloaded belt (reduce load or increase motor), or seized roller creating drag (replace roller). Check each in order, tension is the most common cause.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">When should I replace a conveyor belt?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Replace when you see: edge fraying over 1/2 inch, surface cracks or delamination, visible carcass through the cover, belt stretch beyond tensioner range, splice failure, or hardening/brittleness. For <a href="/industries/food-conveyors/">food belts</a>, also replace when the surface cannot be cleaned to sanitary standards. See <a href="/resources/conveyor-belting/">belt types guide</a> for material-specific life ranges.</p>

</div>
</div>
